; ============================================================================
; Step 10 GDL-I fragment: REPETITION RULE -- ENFORCED BY THE HOST.
;
; RULEBOOK (Repetition Rule): a player may not make a turn that would
; cause a board state to appear FOR THE THIRD TIME during the game. If
; every legal turn would do so, that player loses. A board state is
; everything that determines the legal-move set (piece positions and
; their status flags, boulder state, whose turn it is), with some
; fields counted only when a rule consults them.
;
; THIS FRAGMENT STATES NO RULES FOR IT, ON PURPOSE (issue #421: option
; A of docs/gdl/repetition-encoding.md, chosen 2026-11-27).
;
; WHY. Enforcing the rule needs, for every candidate turn, the IDENTITY
; of the state the turn would produce, compared against every earlier
; state. GDL has no position identity: a description cannot name its
; own state as a value, hash it, or compare two states, except by
; spelling out a successor relation for every move plus a fold of the
; whole board into a term (options B-D in repetition-encoding.md, about
; 250 statements and a per-move cost).
;
; WHO ENFORCES IT. The host: src/ggp/game.py GGPGame counts each
; resulting state in step(), filters third-occurrence moves in
; legal_moves() when `enforce_repetition` is set, and reports the loss
; through all_moves_repetition_blocked(). Set `enforce_repetition=True`
; wherever the GDL game must be the rulebook's game; it is off by
; default (search rollouts leave it off for speed). See
; tests/test_ggp_repetition_host.py.
;
; WHAT WAS HERE BEFORE. A sketch of state-hash counting:
; would_repeat_third_time, legal_after_repetition_filter,
; all_legal_repetition_blocked, no_legal_after_repetition_filter (and a
; `lost` clause through it), a state_repetition_count `next` rule and
; the fluent next_state_hash that fed it. None of it could fire --
; nothing ever computed next_state_hash or created a
; state_repetition_count fact -- and legal_after_repetition_filter
; tested a hash variable never bound to the move, the same bug #389
; fixed in the Tiny Endgame. It looked like a rule to every reader,
; LGREF included, while doing nothing, so it was removed.
; ============================================================================

(role white)
(role black)

; (init facts and helpers from steps 1-9 carry over.)

; ---- Carry-over terminal + goals (uses step-7 royal-queen lost) -------

(<= terminal (lost white))
(<= terminal (lost black))
(<= (goal white 100) (lost black))
(<= (goal black 100) (lost white))
(<= (goal white 0)   (lost white))
(<= (goal black 0)   (lost black))
